// entity_track_range.go is the per-type client-tracking-range + update-interval table, a 1:1
// port of the values every EntityType carries via its EntityType.Builder chain
// (net.minecraft.world.entity.EntityTypes static{} register(...) calls: each builder invokes
// .clientTrackingRange(N) and, when it overrides the default, .updateInterval(M)). The go-mc
// generated data/entity table (DO NOT EDIT) does NOT carry these two fields, so they are
// re-expressed here keyed by the generated entity.<Type>.ID -- the authoritative source is the
// jar bytecode (temp/cache/26.2-inner.jar), NOT the community wiki.
//
// The two numbers drive the two vanilla tracker fidelity knobs the flat `trackRange = 6` const
// (tracker.go) collapsed:
//
//   - clientTrackingRange (in CHUNKS): the entity's visibility radius. ChunkMap.addEntity computes
//     range = type.clientTrackingRange() * 16 (blocks); ChunkMap.TrackedEntity.updatePlayer tracks
//     the entity for a player when dx*dx + dz*dz <= min(range, viewDistance*16)^2 (Euclidean,
//     horizontal). A type with clientTrackingRange 0 (marker) is NEVER tracked (addEntity returns
//     early when range == 0).
//   - updateInterval (in TICKS): ServerEntity.sendChanges runs its move/rot body ONLY when
//     tickCount % updateInterval == 0 (|| needsSync || entityData.isDirty()). Most mobs use 3; items/
//     xp/falling_block/tnt 20; arrows 20; projectiles 10; the always-static decorations (painting,
//     item_frame, lightning, area_effect_cloud, end_crystal) use Integer.MAX_VALUE (never a periodic
//     move send -- they move only on an explicit needsSync teleport). Players/mannequin 2; displays 1.
//
//	[VERIFIED javap net.minecraft.world.entity.EntityType$Builder: default clientTrackingRange = 5,
//	 default updateInterval = 3. javap net.minecraft.world.entity.EntityTypes static{}: every
//	 register(ResourceKey, Builder) chain's .clientTrackingRange(N)/.updateInterval(M) args parsed
//	 from the bytecode (bipush/sipush/iconst before each Builder.clientTrackingRange:(I)/
//	 updateInterval:(I) invokevirtual). javap ChunkMap.addEntity: range = clientTrackingRange()*16,
//	 return when 0. javap ChunkMap$TrackedEntity.updatePlayer: d = min(getEffectiveRange(),
//	 viewDistance*16); track when dx^2+dz^2 <= d^2. getEffectiveRange = scaledRange(range);
//	 getScaledTrackingDistance default multiplier 1.0 (range unchanged).]

// trackUpdateNever is EntityType's Integer.MAX_VALUE updateInterval -- the "never send a periodic
// move" sentinel the always-static decorations (painting, item_frame, glow_item_frame, leash_knot,
// lightning_bolt, area_effect_cloud, end_crystal) carry. With tickCount % Integer.MAX_VALUE only
// == 0 at tickCount 0, such an entity broadcasts a move component solely on its first sendChanges
// and thereafter only on an explicit needsSync teleport (never a drift re-anchor from AI motion).
const trackUpdateNever = 2147483647

// trackParams is one EntityType's (clientTrackingRange, updateInterval) pair -- the Builder args.
// Range is in CHUNKS (multiply by 16 for the block radius); interval is in TICKS.
type trackParams struct {
	rangeChunks    int
	updateInterval int
}

